## Problem solving process analysis

The question asks: How many more marbles did Josh lose than those he found?
- Number of marbles found: {found_num}
- Number of marbles lost: {lost_num}
- The difference between marbles lost and marbles found is {lost_num} - {found_num}

## Actual analysis and solution process

In this question, {found_num} = 9 and {lost_num} = 23.
The question asks how many more marbles were lost than found.
So we calculate: 23 - 9 = 14
The answer is 14
